The '''Byrakan Wars''' were a series of military conflicts fought between the [[Ottelians]] and the [[Byrakans]] between {{abbr|455 BCE|378 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}} and {{abbr|425 BCE|353 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. During these wars, the Ottelians subdued [[Byrak]], a vast territory stretching from the [[GEOGRAPHIC PLACE]] to the [[GEOGRAPHIC PLACE]] in [[Northern Meran]]. The wars culminated in the [[Battle of Usuf]] in {{abbr|425 BCE|353 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, during the [[Third Byrakan War]], where the Ottelians crushed organized Byrakan resistance. This decisive Ottelian victory led to the expansion of [[Ottelia]] over all of [[Byrak]]. 

Byrak had great military importance for the Ottelians, who had suffered several attacks from barbarian tribes originating from both [[Byrak]] and other northern regions of [[Meran]]. The conquest of these territories allowed Ottelia to secure the natural border of [[MOUNTAIN CHAIN]] (?). 

According to [[OTTELIAN HISTORIAN]], the results of the wars were 500 conquered cities, 250 subdued tribes, 300,000 prisoners sold as slaves and another 700,000 killed in battle. It is estimated that the Byrakan population was about 3 to 5 million inhabitants before the war. As a result, the Byrakan Wars are considered one of the deadliest conflicts by percentage of a country's population lost. 

==Background==
Ottelians are imperialists. Byrakans are a growing threat and their land is strategic. 

==First Byrakan War ({{abbr|455 BCE|378 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}} to {{abbr|444 BCE|369 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}})==
Stalemate; [[SOMEONE]] becomes a Byrakan hero and godlike figure in [[Scildism]], but dies shortly after the war. 

==Second Byrakan War ({{abbr|438 BCE|364 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}} to {{abbr|433 BCE|360 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}})==
Ottelian victory; chunk of land occupied. 

==Third Byrakan War ({{abbr|427 BCE|355 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}} to {{abbr|425 BCE|353 BCE (Earth Year Equivalent)}})==
Ottelian victory; Byrak fully annexed. 

==Aftermath==
Byrak fully annexed, occupied by Ottelia and Ottelianized for the next {{abbr|600 years|500 years (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 

